# The toolchain is Linux-side (container) and the tree is 136-files LF against
# a handful of CRLF accidents authored on the Windows host. Normalise on commit
# so a Windows-side edit of a doc or source file cannot produce a whole-file
# diff, and so `make format`'s clang-format output never fights the checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated assembly and the expected/ SHA baselines: byte-exact inputs, never
# hand-edited, and nothing should rewrite them on checkout.
asm/**    -text
expected/** -text
